sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Req as Requester / Agent Owner
    participant SN as ServiceNow (Catalog, Flow Designer, Approvals)
    participant CMDB as ServiceNow CMDB (AI Agent CI)
    participant OMS as Onboarding Microservice (Managed Identity)
    participant State as State Store (Idempotency, Saga Log, Audit)
    participant UCF as Use-Case Framework (Criticality x Role)
    participant Entra as Microsoft Entra ID (Agent ID, App Reg, SP)
    participant KV as Azure Key Vault
    participant APIM as Azure API Management
    participant MCPGW as AI Gateway / MCP Gateway (Tools + A2A)
    participant EntApp as Enterprise Apps / Tool APIs
    participant Oasis as Oasis NHI Platform
    participant Wiz as Wiz (Posture Management)
    participant OTel as OTel Collector (Dynatrace, Splunk)

    Note over Req,OTel: All components emit OpenTelemetry with traceparent = onboarding correlation ID. Collector exports traces and metrics to Dynatrace, logs to Splunk

    Note over Req,UCF: Phase 1 - Intake and classification
    Req->>SN: Submit form: name, purpose, origin (Agent 365 or Claude), runtime host, envs, owner + backup owner, role (supervisor or worker), tools requested, data classification, autonomy level, use-case ID
    SN->>CMDB: Create AI Agent CI (status = Requested, correlation ID)
    SN->>OMS: POST /agents/classify (OAuth client credentials or mTLS)
    OMS->>UCF: Evaluate criticality (complexity x availability x data sensitivity) and role
    UCF-->>OMS: Onboarding profile: tier, approval chain, credential type, rate-limit tier, guardrail set, telemetry level, test depth, recertification cadence, delegation rules
    OMS->>State: Store profile version + correlation ID
    OMS-->>SN: Profile + required approvals

    Note over SN,CMDB: Phase 2 - Tier-driven approval
    alt Tier = Critical
        SN->>SN: Owner manager, security architecture, data owner, CAB (Prod)
    else Tier = Standard
        SN->>SN: Owner manager, security
    else Tier = Low
        SN->>SN: Owner manager only
    end
    SN->>CMDB: CI status = Approved
    SN->>OMS: POST /agents/onboard (correlation ID, idempotency key, profile version)
    OMS-->>SN: 202 Accepted (job ID)

    activate OMS
    OMS->>State: Record job, check idempotency key, lock profile version

    Note over OMS,KV: Phase 3 - Identity (one identity per agent per environment)
    alt Origin = Microsoft Agent 365
        OMS->>Entra: Graph - verify Agent ID, blueprint, sponsor, owner, env
        Entra-->>OMS: Agent object ID and app ID (confirmed, not assumed)
    else Origin = Claude or external
        OMS->>Entra: Create agent identity (Agent ID or App Reg + SP), owner, sponsor, tags (env, tier, role, CI ID, use-case ID)
        alt Runtime hosted on Azure
            OMS->>Entra: Bind managed identity or federated credential (no secret)
        else Runtime outside Azure
            OMS->>Entra: Federated credential if OIDC issuer available, else certificate
            OMS->>KV: Store certificate, rotation policy per tier, grant agent Get only
        end
        Entra-->>OMS: Agent client ID and object ID
    end
    OMS->>Entra: Assign least-privilege app roles and scopes on APIM and tool APIs
    OMS->>Entra: Apply Conditional Access for workload identities (Critical tier, where licensed)
    OMS->>State: Checkpoint - identity complete

    Note over OMS,EntApp: Phase 4 - Runtime enforcement per environment
    loop Each approved environment (dev, qa, uat, prod)
        OMS->>APIM: Product + subscription, validate-jwt (aud, iss, appid or azp, roles), rate-limit tier, correlation header, OTel diagnostics
        APIM-->>OMS: 200 or 201
        OMS->>MCPGW: Register agent client ID, tool allow-list, per-tool scopes, guardrail set, token exchange rules
        alt Role = Supervisor
            OMS->>MCPGW: Bind allowed worker agent IDs (workers must be Active), max delegation depth, on-behalf-of rules
        else Role = Worker
            OMS->>MCPGW: Allow invocation only from approved supervisors, deny agent-to-agent calls outward
        end
        MCPGW-->>OMS: Agent registered
    end
    OMS->>State: Checkpoint - gateways complete

    Note over OMS,Wiz: Phase 5 - Governance and posture
    OMS->>Oasis: Register or enrich agent: object ID, owner, CI ID, tier, role, tools, envs (verify Oasis API, else rely on Entra discovery + tags)
    Oasis->>Entra: Discover identity, entitlements, credentials
    Oasis-->>OMS: Under governance (baseline posture)
    Wiz->>Entra: Connector scan - identity, entitlements
    Wiz->>APIM: Connector scan - Azure resource configuration
    Note over Wiz: Wiz discovers via cloud connectors, it is not an OTel sink
    OMS->>State: Checkpoint - governance complete

    Note over OMS,EntApp: Phase 6 - Verification (depth per tier)
    OMS->>Entra: Acquire token as agent
    OMS->>APIM: Test call with agent token
    APIM->>MCPGW: Forward
    MCPGW->>EntApp: Allowed tool call
    EntApp-->>MCPGW: 200 OK
    MCPGW-->>OMS: Allowed call OK, disallowed tool denied
    opt Tier = Critical
        OMS->>MCPGW: Guardrail tests, delegation tests, failover check
    end
    OMS->>OTel: Confirm trace arrived for smoke test
    deactivate OMS

    alt All steps succeeded
        OMS->>SN: Callback - success, IDs per env, APIM product, MCP registration, Oasis ID, profile version
        SN->>CMDB: CI status = Active, relationships (owner, APIM, MCP, Oasis, supervisor-worker)
        SN-->>Req: Onboarded notification
    else Any step failed
        OMS->>OMS: Compensate in reverse (MCP, APIM, role assignments, credentials, identity)
        OMS->>OTel: Failure event with step and reason
        OMS->>SN: Callback - failed, step, reason
        SN->>CMDB: CI status = Failed
        SN-->>Req: Failure notice + incident
    end

    Note over Req,OTel: Phase 7 - Day-2 lifecycle
    Oasis->>SN: NHI findings - excess permissions, stale agent, owner departed, credential aging
    Wiz->>SN: Posture findings - misconfiguration, exposure, toxic combinations
    SN->>OMS: Change, recertify (cadence per tier), or offboard request
    OMS->>MCPGW: Deregister agent, remove supervisor-worker bindings
    OMS->>APIM: Revoke subscription
    OMS->>Entra: Remove roles, disable then delete identity
    OMS->>KV: Revoke certificate
    OMS->>SN: CI status = Retired
